# HBr dissociative gas uptake; Sander (2023), CC-BY-4.0, note 146.
# Source: https://doi.org/10.5194/acp-23-10901-2023
# Changes: concentration/Pa basis converted to molal/atm using USGS pure-water
# density; reference enthalpy derived from the source slope and density slope.
# See provenance/sander-2023-hbr-review.md. The delta_h is a DERIVED LOCAL
# reference-temperature slope, not a measured calorimetric value. Away from
# 298.15 K this constant-enthalpy continuation requires an explicit boundary.
PHASES
HBr(g)
    HBr = H+ + Br-
    log_k 8.922102677041854
    delta_h -82.76420684218871 kJ/mol
